.TH pvc-delayfilter 1  "pvc-delayfilter " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-delayfilter \- Per\-bin time\-delay resynthesis: reads a source `.pva` file and, for each frequency bin, fetches its source frame from a bin\-specific point earlier in the source\*(Aqs own timeline \- the per\-bin delay times (and amp multipliers) come from a `groupdelaymaker`\-produced response file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-delayfilter\fR [\fB\-\-window\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR] [\fB\-\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-delay\-time\-scaler\fR] [\fB\-\-pitch\fR] [\fB\-\-freq\-shift\fR] [\fB\-\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-time\-origin\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-delay\-transpose\fR] [\fB\-\-delay\-shift\fR] [\fB\-\-delay\-warpshape\fR] [\fB\-\-zero\-delay\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-delay\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-delay\-gain\-curve\fR] [\fB\-\-delay\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-comp\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-comp\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-attack\fR] [\fB\-\-freq\-response\-time\fR] [\fB\-\-warp\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-threshold\fR] <\fB\-\-delay\-filter\fR> [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIANALYSIS\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Per\-bin time\-delay resynthesis: reads a source `.pva` file and, for each frequency bin, fetches its source frame from a bin\-specific point earlier in the source\*(Aqs own timeline \- the per\-bin delay times (and amp multipliers) come from a `groupdelaymaker`\-produced response file.
.PP
Ports `delayfilter`\*(Aqs audio\-processing path (`legacy/pvc_src/ delayfilter.c`); see `pvc\-core::tools::delayfilter`\*(Aqs doc comment for what\*(Aqs in and out of scope, including a real `\-C` flag whose own numeric value is never actually used by the original tool.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-size\fR \fI<WINDOW_SIZE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-M`: analysis/resynthesis window length. `0` means auto (`2 * fft`, where `fft` is always the source file\*(Aqs own FFT size \- `delayfilter` has no independent `\-\-fft`)
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<WINDOW>\fR [default: hamming]

.TP
\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR \fI<FRAMES_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 200]
`\-D`: output frames per second (sets the hop size). Values under `32` reset to `200`, matching the C\*(Aqs own safety clamp
.TP
\fB\-\-duration\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 0]
`\-d`: output duration in seconds. `0` (the default) means "use the source file\*(Aqs own analysis duration" (before the delay tail is added \- see `pvc\-core::tools::delayfilter`\*(Aqs doc comment on `func_dur` vs `dur`)
.TP
\fB\-\-delay\-time\-scaler\fR \fI<DELAY_TIME_SCALER>\fR [default: 0]
`\-x`: scales how much each bin\*(Aqs own delay is applied when time\-shifting that bin\*(Aqs control\-function lookups (`0` = no shift, `1` = full shift) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-pitch\fR \fI<PITCH>\fR [default: 0]
`\-P`: pitch shift in semitones \- a plain number, or `@path`. Nonzero (or time\-varying, with `\-\-freq\-shift`) picks oscillator\-bank resynthesis; both left at `0` picks overlap\-add
.TP
\fB\-\-freq\-shift\fR \fI<FREQ_SHIFT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-a`: frequency shift in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-gain\fR \fI<GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-A`: gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-time\-origin\fR \fI<TIME_ORIGIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-Q`: source time\-position origin in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\fR \fI<RATE>\fR [default: 1]
`\-Y`: source navigation rate multiplier \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-delay\-transpose\fR \fI<DELAY_TRANSPOSE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-b`: pitch transposition of the group\-delay response, in semitones \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-delay\-shift\fR \fI<DELAY_SHIFT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-e`: frequency shift of the group\-delay response, in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-delay\-warpshape\fR \fI<DELAY_WARPSHAPE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-w`: warp index for reshaping the group\-delay response. Truncated to an integer, matching the original tool\*(Aqs own `(int)` cast on this one flag (see `pvc\-core::tools::delayfilter`\*(Aqs doc comment)
.TP
\fB\-\-zero\-delay\-gain\fR \fI<ZERO_DELAY_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-V`: decibel gain applied to a bin with zero delay \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-delay\-gain\fR \fI<MAX_DELAY_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-y`: decibel gain applied to a bin at the maximum delay \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-delay\-gain\-curve\fR \fI<DELAY_GAIN_CURVE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-z`: curve shape (warp index) of the zero\-to\-max delay gain interpolation \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-delay\-window\fR \fI<DELAY_WINDOW>\fR [default: 0]
`\-T`: multiplier applied to every bin\*(Aqs own delay time (also sizes the output\*(Aqs extra ring\-out tail) \- a plain number, or `@path`. Real default is `0` (no delay applied at all) \- the original tool\*(Aqs own `usage()` text claims `[1.]`, but its actual initializer sets this control function\*(Aqs constant to `0.`; the documented default doesn\*(Aqt match the real one, confirmed by reading both. Reproduced here rather than "corrected" to `1`
.TP
\fB\-\-comp\-threshold\fR \fI<COMP_THRESHOLD>\fR [default: 0]
`\-E`: input spectrum compression threshold in dB (must be `<= 0`)
.TP
\fB\-\-comp\-db\fR \fI<COMP_DB>\fR [default: 0]
`\-c`: input spectrum decibels of compression (must be `<= 0`)
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR \fI<RELEASE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-L`: output envelope release time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-attack\fR \fI<ATTACK>\fR [default: 0]
`\-l`: output envelope attack time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-freq\-response\-time\fR \fI<FREQ_RESPONSE_TIME>\fR [default: 0]
`\-f`: output frequency change response time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-warp\fR \fI<WARP>\fR [default: 0]
`\-W`: input spectrum magnitude warp index \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-H`: low shelf EQ gain in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-X`: high shelf EQ gain in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_FREQ>\fR [default: 200]
`\-m`: low shelf EQ frequency in Hz
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_FREQ>\fR [default: 2000]
`\-R`: high shelf EQ frequency in Hz
.TP
\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fI<THRESHOLD>\fR [default: \-60]
`\-t`: oscillator resynthesis threshold in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-delay\-filter\fR \fI<DELAY_FILTER>\fR
`\-B`: path to the group\-delay response file (a `groupdelaymaker` `.fr`\-shaped file of per\-bin `(amp, delay\-seconds)` pairs). Required
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIANALYSIS\fR>
`\-F`: path to the source `.pva` analysis file to resynthesize from
.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>

